  "question": {
    "text": "P-T diagram of an ideal gas having three different densities $\\rho_1, \\rho_2, \\rho_3$ (in three different cases) is shown in the figure. Which of the following is correct :\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/FY3RknQd1DR5i3YKub5pOiXUSbj4Xn7hbwpUytlXyE8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GQWhG",
      "text": "$\\rho_1>\\rho_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wGPaW",
      "text": "$\\rho_2 < \\rho_3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UBg46",
      "text": "$\\rho_1=\\rho_2=\\rho_3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vYxO3",
      "text": "$\\rho_1 < \\rho_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For ideal gas\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& P V=n R T \\\\\n& P V=\\frac{m}{M} R T \\\\\n& P=\\left(\\frac{M}{V}\\right) \\frac{R T}{M} \\\\\n& P=\\frac{\\rho R T}{M}\n\\end{aligned}$\n(Where $\\mathrm{m}$ is mass of gas and $\\mathrm{M}$ is molecular mass of gas)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/sB72bMqLldNuXVQOFMuzIj48-a6mJ8Tb91CeUaR8zt0.original.fullsize.png\"><br />for same temperature $\\mathrm{P}_1>\\mathrm{P}_2>\\mathrm{P}_3$\nSo $\\rho_1>\\rho_2>\\rho_3$",
    "image": null
  },
